<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish NTMA to auction 150 mln punts of 10-yr bond.</title>
<headline>Irish NTMA to auction 150 mln punts of 10-yr bond.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's National Treasury Management Agency (NTMA) said on Tuesday that it would auction 150 million Irish pounds of the eight percent Treasury bond due 2006 in a competitive auction on April 15.</p>
<p>The auction, which will be held at 1000 local time (0900 GMT) and confined to primary dealers, will be followed by a non-competitive auction of up to 30 million Irish pounds which will also be confined to primary dealers, the NTMA said.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
